The FAQ, quite deliberately, says neither "thou shalt not spoil" nor
"thou shouldst expect not to be spoiled". It suggests that those
posting spoilers _may_ wish to hide or flag those spoilers, and
indicates some preferred means of doing so if that's the case; and
warns that readers of the newsgroup should expect to see spoilers.

If people want to avoid spoilers, then they have two options: most
surely, don't read the group; or make it clear in a post that you
would like spoilery responses _in that thread_ to be avoided or
concealed, and restrict your reading to that thread. (Krysia's
Krusader followed the latter approach in the Ellora threads, and it
seemed to work pretty well.)

